github:github/gh-aw#46835.body:
`isCoreAliasIdentifier` rejected any binding with `def.type !== "Variable"`, silently disabling `require-return-after-core-setfailed`, `no-core-exportvariable-non-string`, and `no-core-setoutput-non-string` for the dependency-injection pattern where `core` is passed as a function argument.

## Changes

- **`core-method-resolve.ts` — `isCoreAliasIdentifier`**: adds a `"Parameter"` branch that accepts plain (non-destructured) function parameters whose name is in `CORE_ALIASES`. Gated on exact `CORE_ALIASES` membership (`"core"` | `"coreObj"`) to avoid treating arbitrary parameter names as core.

```js
// Now flagged — `core` parameter recognized as core alias
function g(core) {
  core.setFailed("bad");  // ← missingReturnAfterSetFailed
  doMore();
}

// Still NOT flagged — `coreArg` not in CORE_ALIASES (shadow-exclusion preserved)
function g(coreArg) {
  coreArg.setFailed("bad");
  doMore();
}
```

- **Tests** — adds parameter-DI invalid cases and shadow-exclusion valid cases to all three affected rule test suites (`require-return-after-core-setfailed`, `no-core-exportvariable-non-string`, `no-core-setoutput-non-string`).

<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->

- Fixes #46734

